      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "pkgs/billing/src/billing/tax.py",
      "line_number": 8,
      "line_end": 8,
      "title": "None return breaks both tax_for callers",
      "description": "For an unknown region, tax_for now returns None instead of 0. Both callers do arithmetic on the result without checking for None. For any region missing from RATES, order_total in checkout.py raises TypeError on int plus None. The same input makes tax_line in receipt.py raise TypeError on None divided by 100, so checkout and receipts crash. Keep returning 0 for unknown regions. Otherwise, update order_total and tax_line to handle None in the same change.",
      "suggested_change": "        return 0",
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "For an unknown region, tax_for now returns None instead of 0. Both callers do arithmetic on the result without checking for None.",
